---
/**
 * TocAnchor — marks where in a post's body the sticky TOC sidebar (`PostToc.astro`)
 * should start appearing, instead of the top of the post body (the default).
 *
 * Drop it in the MDX/MD content at the point the TOC should "begin" — after an
 * intro paragraph, before a video, wherever:
 *
 *   ## Introduction
 *   A few paragraphs the TOC shouldn't cover yet...
 *
 *   <TocAnchor />
 *
 *   ## The real content
 *   ...
 *
 * Renders nothing visible — it's a zero-size marker `PostToc` measures at
 * runtime (browsers don't exist at Astro build time, so this can't be a
 * build-time offset; see `PostToc.astro`'s script). Optional: omit it and the
 * TOC starts at the top of the body, as before.
 *
 * Plain `.md` posts (no component imports) can use the same mechanism without
 * this component — raw HTML passes through Markdown verbatim, so
 * `<span data-toc-anchor></span>` dropped directly in the body works
 * identically. This component is just the `.mdx` sugar for it.
 */
---
<span data-toc-anchor aria-hidden="true"></span>

<style>
  span[data-toc-anchor] {
    display: block;
    height: 0;
    width: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
</style>
